Note on game assets: NMS Galactic Map is a fan-made portal decoder and 3D
galaxy map for No Man's Sky. This license covers the original code
(preview.html, the Netlify Functions, nms-tools/, and the address/generation
logic in nms-core/ -- see the third-party note below for what in nms-core/
is and isn't elegra1965's own work) in this project only. The portal glyphs,
race/economy icons, and other imagery sourced or adapted from No Man's Sky
itself are the property of Hello Games and are not covered by this license
-- they're included here under fair-use fan-project conventions. Anyone
reusing this code should credit elegra1965 for the original work and source
their own copies of any game assets rather than relying on this license to
cover them.

Note on decompiled game data: nms-core/economy.js's probability tables
(abandoned/empty/outlaw system odds, ring chance) were decompiled from a
legitimately-owned No Man's Sky install for research and interoperability
purposes, per the note above -- Hello Games owns the underlying game data,
elegra1965's own code is the transcription/lookup logic and the two roll
functions (rollSystemFlavor, rollRing) built around it, not a claim of
authorship over the numbers themselves.

Note on shared data: this license covers the code only, not any community-
submitted system data collected via the live site's Edit system feature
(stored in data/overrides.json on the deployed backend) -- that data belongs
to the players who submitted it.

----------------------------------------------------------------------------

Note on third-party code: all files in nms-core/ except economy.js and
letter-map/ (star type, planet count, black hole/Atlas placement, and
system/region/planet name generation) are a port of hadsh/nms_namegen
(https://github.com/hadsh/nms_namegen), itself a fork of Stuart Coyle's
original nms_namegen, co-authored by GoodGuysFree. hadsh's repository
states this work is MIT-licensed. The MIT license above applies to
elegra1965's own original code in this project; it does not make elegra1965
the author of the ported generation logic. Each ported file under nms-core/
additionally carries its own "Ported from hadsh/nms_namegen (MIT licensed)"
attribution comment at the top, per MIT's own requirement that the original
notice travel with the code. Credit for the underlying generation
algorithms belongs to Stuart Coyle (original author), GoodGuysFree
(co-author of the hadsh fork), and hadsh (fork maintainer).

nms-core/economy.js (real system economy/conflict/race odds and ring
generation, added 2026-08-12) and everything in nms-tools/ (the
nms-lookup.js single-call wrapper, added 2026-08-15) are elegra1965's own
original code, not ported from hadsh's work -- the upstream nms_namegen
project never modeled economy/conflict/race/rings at all, so there was
nothing to port for that part. Both are covered by the MIT license above
like the rest of this project's own code, subject to the decompiled-data
note further up.
